# GROUPS file.
# Defines GROUPS and HOSTS.  The concept is that HOSTS in the same
# GROUP have an equation tying them together with an intrinsic
# dispersion SIGMA.
# Each HOST has a distance modulus parameter.  Each GROUP has a
# distance modulus parameter.  Generally there are no additional
# covariances.   SIGMA represents the intrinsic distance modulus
# dispersion of the host with respect to the group; it will generally
# be the same for all group members, but it could differ for hosts
# that are potential outliers.
#
# GROUPNAME    HOSTNAME   SIGMA
Fornax         IC2006     0.057
Fornax         N1344      0.057
Fornax         N1374      0.057
Fornax         N1375      0.057
Fornax         N1380      0.057
Fornax         N1399      0.057
Fornax         N1404      0.057
Virgo          N4458      0.086
Virgo          N4472      0.086
Virgo          N4489      0.086
Virgo          N4552      0.086
Virgo          N4636      0.086
Virgo          N4649      0.086